<article class="env-definition" id="0AKY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AKY">Definition <span data-tag="0AKY">87.20.7</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be a formal algebraic space over $S$. We say $X$ is <em>locally countably indexed</em>, <em>locally countably indexed and classical</em>, <em>locally weakly adic</em>, <em>locally adic*</em>, or <em>locally Noetherian</em> if the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/0AKX" data-tag="0AKX">87.20.6</a> hold for the corresponding property. </p>
</article>